+        Releases each Q / K / V stage once its load completed with valid data. Per work tile the load warp issues
+        Q0, Q1 into Q stages 0, 1 and K0, K1, V0, K2, V1, ..., V(n-1) into the K/V ring, so K/V load j of a tile is
+        K0 (j = 0), V(n-1) (j = 2n-1), K((j+1)/2) (odd j) or V(j/2-1) (even j). A stage is refilled only after the
+        MMA and this warp both released it, so the loads in flight lie in [base, base + kv_stage). Bit s of
+        ``kv_done`` marks stage s's load in that window as released; bit s of ``kv_parity`` / ``q_parity`` is the
+        parity of the primary phase stage s completes next. Every completion flips the primary phase, valid or not,
+        while the conditional phase the MMA waits on completes only with valid data. An invalid stage is re-armed
+        and re-loaded with report_valid into the same stage and revisited on the next sweep, so several stages can
